                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7bd8cd8f-c74b-3731-bb91-ef10d2bfb3aa",
                        "entry_id": "48d931ed-cf38-399c-93b0-3dca46fc9cc9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "церк. один из основных отличительных элементов богослужебного одеяния епископа, представляющий собой широкую ленту, изначально из шерсти, позже из шёлка, атласа и других материалов, которая охватывает плечи, при этом один её конец спускается на грудь, а другой - на спину"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aaf82e12-e931-4af7-87c9-ec2b4e62e789",
                                "sense_id": "7bd8cd8f-c74b-3731-bb91-ef10d2bfb3aa",
                                "text": "В такие моменты чин архиерейского служения обязывает архиерея отлагать омофор ― древнейший и главный отличительный символ архиерейского сана. Омофор отлагается во время чтения Священного Писания. Но также омофор отлагается и во время совершения анафоры. Малый омофор одевается только во время произнесения установительных слов Спасителя «Приимите ядите. Приимите, пейте.» и эпиклезы, затем вновь отлагается."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f6446103-dae6-4227-b6b3-d57168ac89a2",
                        "source_entry_id": "48d931ed-cf38-399c-93b0-3dca46fc9cc9",
                        "source_sense_id": "7bd8cd8f-c74b-3731-bb91-ef10d2bfb3aa",
                        "target_lang_word": "omophorion",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "omophorion",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a658a615-0325-3497-83ed-2f6078fe0915",
                                        "entry_id": "3f82bd08-dccd-3a26-98c1-ccf586dee654",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A band of brocade originally of wool decorated with crosses and worn on the neck and around the shoulders as the distinguishing vestment of a bishop and the symbol of his spiritual and ecclesiastical authority in the Eastern Christian liturgical tradition, equivalent to the Western archepiscopal pallium."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4cb3ef8-a8cb-437f-88d4-dc6561605eec",
                                                "sense_id": "a658a615-0325-3497-83ed-2f6078fe0915",
                                                "text": "a little band of marchers displays Greek Orthodox outfits, the rhason and sticharion, the epitrachelion and the epimanikia, the sakkos, the epigonation, the zone, the omophorion; they brandish icons and enkolpia, dikerotikera and dikanikion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52b0428a-ad10-4444-8edc-6dc615af5225",
                                                "sense_id": "a658a615-0325-3497-83ed-2f6078fe0915",
                                                "text": "The bishop wears an omophorion, whose shape and manner of wearing are closer to the original pallium than either the stole or the epitrachelion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59e68d42-ee96-497e-87a0-fd6a5e1177f5",
                                                "sense_id": "a658a615-0325-3497-83ed-2f6078fe0915",
                                                "text": "Although the bishop also wears - an epitrachelion, his distinctive sign of office is the omophorion-a long, broad strip arranged on the shoulders in such a way that one end descends in front and the other behind. The word 'omophorion' means \"shoulder covering\" and originally referred to a piece of sheepskin worn over the shoulders by the aged and in firm for warmth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e65091f5-0ef4-40fb-9250-9f4b43b88620",
                        "source_entry_id": "48d931ed-cf38-399c-93b0-3dca46fc9cc9",
                        "source_sense_id": "7bd8cd8f-c74b-3731-bb91-ef10d2bfb3aa",
                        "target_lang_word": "gremial",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gremial",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2ddfe2c1-ae07-31ea-ad6d-b912c728a6a4",
                                        "entry_id": "d8a903e5-692c-3e70-a936-a262f2f661bc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to the lap."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "gremial",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1de3eb5c-7073-370e-949f-1dee54713300",
                                        "entry_id": "852731c0-6427-3eb7-8837-7ef5c62c57b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A decorated cloth placed on a bishop's lap whilst celebrating mass or ordaining priests."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "24ce7424-7a66-3b99-ae22-75246902ad25",
                                        "entry_id": "852731c0-6427-3eb7-8837-7ef5c62c57b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bosom friend."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e8b3eea-ea16-49d7-8b3e-ecc213412427",
                                                "sense_id": "24ce7424-7a66-3b99-ae22-75246902ad25",
                                                "text": "These Friars living in these convents were capable of degrees, and kept their Acts, as other University-men. Yet were they gremials and not gremials, who sometimes would so stand on the tiptoes of their privileges, that they endeavoured to be higher than other students: so that oftentimes they and the scholars could not set their horses in one stable, or rather their books on one shelf."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
